A||N||12||Motorhead||0-120 Speedo||||1||
Z||000000||Motorhead||02-06-2000||06:00 AM||||<BR>Does anyone know if the v-6 and 4-cyl spedos are interchangeable?  Specifically. will the 120 speedo replace the 85 mph unit in my '86 coupe||||reg||1
Z||000001||Oreif||02-06-2000||11:10 AM||||Yes, the Speedo's are interchangable I installed an '87 GT speedo in my "86 SE with no problem.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Motorhead||02-06-2000||11:37 AM||||Thanks for the info. thought it was no problem.||||reg||1
Z||000003||batboy||02-06-2000||11:54 AM||||The tach is different between the 4 and 6 cylinders, but not the speedo.||||reg||1
Z||000004||TOM||02-06-2000||10:04 PM||||Not all the lighting is the same. All the 120's are backlit but not all the clusters are. I dont think any of the 4 cyl clusters are||||reg||1
Z||000005||fierodave||02-06-2000||10:49 PM||||Tom  are you sure?<BR>I have a backlit and a 4-cyl cluster in my hands the only thing i see that needs to be done is a hole drilled out in the cluster plastic on the back side to let the speed-o electronic's fit!<BR>the light bulbs shine through the same holes, and i think the speed-o itself spreads out the light,  <BR>I may be way off but as  I look at them, this is what i see!  TOM  your the expert,  please check it out and let me know too. I have a guy wanting to buy my 120   he had the same question  thanks all for the space<BR>FD<p>[This message has been edited by fierodave (edited 02-06-2000).]||||reg||10
Z||000006||FIEROCIOUS||02-06-2000||11:32 PM||||The tach filter used on GM products consists of a capacitor and a resistor. You can change from 4,6 or 8 simply by changing th capacitor. 4=0.01uF    6=0.0082uF and<BR>8=0.0064uF capacitor values are in micro farads. It is located on top of the tachs circuit board. (looks like a silver cylinder with wires coming out each side)Support your local Raidioshack! ||||reg||7
Z||000007||JetroGT||02-07-2000||12:18 AM||||I have a delema. <BR>I have the complete 120 gauge cluster. But the circuit board on the 120 gauge was fried. I tried to take the circuit board from the 86SE gauges, "which are exactly the same as the GT gauges except that the SE gauges only go up to 80" and the speed was way off. Both the gauges came from V6 cars. Whats the Difference? Is it the crystal? All of the parts were the same.||||reg||5
Z||000008||ggarsk||02-07-2000||02:11 AM||||I just put the 120 speedo, tach and rally gauges in my '84. The tach is about 100 rpm off from the original. The backlit gauges are so much nicer...easier to see at night.||||reg||1
Z||000009||TOM||02-07-2000||10:49 AM||||The backlit guages have a seal to keep the light from coming around the face. If you also swap the seal I think they will work. But without doing the other guages you will have different looks. Or paint the back of the speedo and make it a reflector type||||reg||1
Z||000010||superXmotorsports||02-08-2000||06:41 PM||||My friend Ron Smigla, who is also on this forum, has the V6 set in his 84 Indy and he said they work fine.  I have a 4cyl cluster here  that I'm going to dismantle to see how it works.  I'm trying to get the gauge manufacturers to make a set for the 4cyl.  SXM.||||reg||1
Z||000011||Motorhead||02-08-2000||07:10 PM||||WOW!  Thanks for all the responses guys.  Go ahead and call me a neophyte, but after all the discussion, all I have are more questions.<P>So far, seems as though installing the speed-o is no problem as far as function is concerned. However, if the thing is going to look like a high school cheerleader in a house of ill repute because of lighting, I think I'll pass.<P>As an old English sports car driver, whose instruments were lit by a bulb stuck in the back of the case, or a flashlight, cuz Lucas electrics were a mystery even to Old Man Lucas himself, I can't quite distinguish the different lighting configurations we seem to be discussing.  Does backlit mean the instrument face is translucent, and allows the light to pass through it?  Is the alternative the old bulb in the back of the case?<P>Help me here ya'll, Never saw a "peanut" bulb 'till I started replacing bulbs in this car.<P>Little suckers put out alot of light for their size, don't they?<P>The Old Fart thanks you for your enlightenment!||||reg||1
Z||000012||Standard||02-09-2000||01:17 AM||||You're guessed good about backlit gauges.  The light shines through transparent parts of the gauges, i.e. the numbers and dashes.    <BR>Reflector type gauges use a reflector to make the light shine on the front of the gauge.  Not as bright as backlit gauges.<P>Reflector type was found in 84's and 85's(?), and I think it was all backlit from 86 to 88.  I think every car nowadays uses backlit gauges, because they are so much easier to read.<BR>Always willing to help an old fart out!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>feel free to correct me if I'm wrong, everybody.||||reg||1
